#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:1
msgid "Source pages, source links and class diagrams"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:4
msgid "Five of Sphinx's built-in extensions connect a manual to the code it describes and to the build that makes it. ``viewcode`` writes a highlighted copy of each documented module and links it with the descriptions. ``linkcode`` links each description to its source on the web. ``inheritance_diagram`` draws class graphs. ``duration`` reports which documents are slow to read. ``imgconverter`` makes sure every image reaches the book."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:6
msgid "We turn them on as in Sphinx, by name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:17
msgid "The first three read Python source with the same scan that autodoc uses (:doc:`autodoc`). Nothing is imported, and no program runs. The scan finds a module below ``autodoc_source_paths``, its classes and functions, their bases, and the lines each one spans. A description written by hand with ``py:class`` or ``py:function`` is found as well as one that autodoc wrote, as long as its module is below those folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:21
msgid "Python source is read by the source scan while documents are read. The scan gives each Python description its file and lines, and each inheritance diagram its classes. When pages are written, the lines become source links and source pages, and the classes become a Graphviz drawing whose nodes link to the descriptions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:21
msgid "Reading finds where each object is defined; writing turns that into links, pages and drawings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:42
msgid "Every Python file the scan reads is a dependency of the document that needed it. When we edit a module, the documents that describe it are read again, and their links, source pages and diagrams follow the edit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:44
msgid "Source pages: viewcode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:47
msgid "With ``sphinx.ext.viewcode`` listed, each Python description gets a ``[source]`` link after its signature. The link leads to a page that shows the module's source, highlighted like any code block. On that page each described class and function sits in a block with a ``[docs]`` link back to its description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:49
msgid "For this module, ``src/shapes.py``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:60
msgid "the description of ``shapes.Square`` links to ``_modules/shapes.html#Square``, and the source page links back to ``index.html#shapes.Square``. A page for each module lies in ``_modules/<package>/<module>.html``, and ``_modules/index.html`` lists them all, a package's modules nested inside it. The links are relative, so they work under ``dirhtml`` and when we open the files straight from the disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:62
msgid "A class that a package re-exports is linked to the module that defines it. If ``Square`` were defined in ``shapes/square.py`` and imported by ``shapes/__init__.py``, the description of ``shapes.Square`` would link to ``_modules/shapes/square.html#Square``. A block starts at the definition's first decorator and ends at its last line, so a decorated method shows its decorators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:64
msgid "The settings have Sphinx's names and defaults:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:66
msgid "``viewcode_follow_imported_members``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:67
msgid "``true`` (default): link a re-exported object to the module that defines it. ``false``: link only objects that the named module defines itself. The old name ``viewcode_import`` is read as this setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:69
msgid "``viewcode_line_numbers``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:70
msgid "``false`` (default). ``true`` numbers the lines of the source pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:72
msgid "``viewcode_enable_epub``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:73
msgid "Accepted and unused, since Guidedog has no EPUB builder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:75
msgid "Source pages exist in ``html`` and ``dirhtml`` only, as in Sphinx. ``singlehtml``, the PDF and text have neither the links nor the pages: a book does not need a second copy of the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:77
msgid "A description whose module is not below ``autodoc_source_paths`` gets no link. The note ``viewcode.source`` names the module once per document, with the hint to add its folder. A module file larger than 8 MiB, the limit of every source read, gets no page, with the warning ``viewcode.limit``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:79
msgid "Source links on the web: linkcode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:82
msgid "Sphinx's ``linkcode`` calls a Python function, ``linkcode_resolve``, to make each link. Guidedog never runs Python, so it takes a URL template instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:89
msgid "In a repository whose checked-out branch is ``main``, the description of ``Square.area`` above then links to ``https://github.com/acme/shapes/blob/main/src/shapes.py#L4-L6``. These placeholders are filled for each object:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:91
msgid "Placeholders of ``linkcode_url``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:95
msgid "Placeholder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:96
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:97
msgid "``{domain}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:98
msgid "The object's domain: ``py``, ``c``, ``cpp``, ``js``, ``rust``, ``odin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:99
msgid "``{module}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:100
msgid "The module as the description names it, or the Rust or Odin crate or package path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:101
msgid "``{fullname}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:102
msgid "The object's name within its module, such as ``Square.area``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:103
msgid "``{path}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:104
msgid "The object's source file, relative to ``linkcode_root``, with ``/`` between folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:105
msgid "``{line}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:106
msgid "The first line of the definition, counted from 1. A decorator's line counts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:107
msgid "``{end_line}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:108
msgid "The last line of the definition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:109
msgid "``{branch}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:110
msgid "``linkcode_branch``, or the branch read from the repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:111
msgid "``{{`` and ``}}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:112
msgid "A literal brace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:114
msgid "``linkcode_root`` names the folder ``{path}`` is relative to, relative to the source folder. Left empty, it is the nearest folder at or above the source folder that holds ``.git``. ``linkcode_branch`` is the text of ``{branch}``. Left empty, it is the branch that the repository has checked out, read from ``.git/HEAD``, or the commit when ``HEAD`` is detached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:116
msgid "A link is added only when every placeholder the template uses has a value. A Python object that the scan found has them all. A ``c:`` or ``cpp:`` object, and the objects of the Rust and Odin domains, carry their names but no file. Only a template that uses nothing but ``{domain}``, ``{module}``, ``{fullname}`` and ``{branch}`` links them, for example a template that points at an API search."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:118
msgid "The links appear in HTML builders, ``singlehtml`` included, after the signature and before the permalink. The PDF and text add nothing. With both ``viewcode`` and ``linkcode`` listed, a description gets both links."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:120
msgid "Mistakes in the template are found when ``conf.toml`` loads. An unknown placeholder or an unclosed brace is refused, and listing the extension without ``linkcode_url`` is the warning ``config.ext.linkcode``. A build that needs ``{branch}`` but has no branch and no repository warns ``linkcode.branch`` once and adds no links. An object whose file lies outside ``linkcode_root`` gets no link, with the note ``linkcode.outside``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:122
msgid "``guidedog migrate`` cannot read a ``linkcode_resolve`` function as data. It reports ``migrate.linkcode`` with a template to write in its place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:124
msgid "Class diagrams: inheritance_diagram"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:127
msgid "The ``inheritance-diagram`` directive draws the classes it names, a module's classes when it names a module, and their bases up to the roots:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:134
msgid "The names are found as Sphinx finds them: relative to the current module first (``py:currentmodule``), then as written. The bases are read from the class statements and resolved across the scanned modules. Python's builtins, such as ``object`` and ``Exception``, are not drawn. A base from a package outside the source folders is drawn with its full name and nothing above it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:136
msgid "The directive takes Sphinx's options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:138
msgid "``:parts: N``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:139
msgid "Show only the last ``N`` parts of each dotted name; a negative ``N`` drops the first ``-N`` parts instead. ``0`` (default) shows the full name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:141
msgid "``:private-bases:``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:142
msgid "Draw classes whose names start with ``_`` as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:144
msgid "``:top-classes: a.B, a.C``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:145
msgid "Stop at these classes: their own bases are not drawn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:147
msgid "``:include-subclasses:``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:148
msgid "Draw the classes that derive from the named ones too. The scan looks for them in the packages of the named classes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:150
msgid "``:caption: text``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:151
msgid "Put the drawing in a figure with this caption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:153
msgid "The settings ``inheritance_graph_attrs``, ``inheritance_node_attrs`` and ``inheritance_edge_attrs`` add Graphviz attributes to the graph, its nodes and its edges, and ``inheritance_alias`` shows a full class name as another name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:163
msgid "The graph is written as Sphinx writes it and drawn by the linked Graphviz, like a ``graphviz`` directive, so no ``dot`` program is needed. In HTML the drawing is an SVG with the ``graphviz-adaptive`` colours, and each node links to its class's description when the project has one. A class without a description is drawn without a link. The PDF embeds the same SVG. Text shows the classes as a list, each with its bases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:165
msgid "A name that is neither a class nor a module in the scan is reported as ``inheritance.class`` and left out. A diagram may hold at most 1,000 classes; a larger one is ``inheritance.limit`` and is not drawn. Loading ``conf.toml`` refuses an attribute name that is not a Graphviz identifier, and a value that is not a plain word, number or quoted string is quoted, so an attribute cannot change the rest of the graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:167
msgid "Reading times: duration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:170
msgid "With ``sphinx.ext.duration`` listed, the build summary shows how long reading took, and which documents took longest:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:181
msgid "Each time is measured with a monotonic clock around one document's read. A document taken unchanged from the previous build took no time and is not listed. The output folder also receives ``sphinx-reading-durations.json``, an object from document names to seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:183
msgid "``duration_print_total``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:184
msgid "``true`` (default): show the total reading time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:186
msgid "``duration_print_slowest``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:187
msgid "``true`` (default): show the slowest documents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:189
msgid "``duration_n_slowest``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:190
msgid "How many slowest documents to show: ``5`` by default, ``0`` for all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:192
msgid "``duration_write_json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:193
msgid "The JSON file's name in the output folder; empty writes none. A name that leaves the output folder is refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:195
msgid "``duration_limit``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:196
msgid "Seconds a document may take; a slower one is the warning ``duration.limit``. Unset, there is no limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:198
msgid "The times are evidence about one build on one machine. They differ from run to run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:200
msgid "Images for the book: imgconverter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:203
msgid "Sphinx's ``imgconverter`` runs ImageMagick to turn images LaTeX cannot use, such as GIF and SVG, into ones it can. Guidedog's PDF is typeset by Typst, which reads PNG, JPEG, GIF, SVG, WebP and PDF images directly, so there is nothing to convert. The extension is accepted, and no program is ever started. ``image_converter`` and ``image_converter_args`` are accepted and have no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:205
msgid "An image in a format the book cannot show, such as TIFF or BMP, is reported as ``imgconverter.format``, and the book shows its alternative text in its place. The hint suggests a PNG, JPEG, GIF or SVG version. When we name the image ``picture.*``, each output picks the first version it reads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:207
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../sources-and-diagrams.rst:210
msgid "Every message has a code, the location, an explanation and a hint. ``suppress_warnings`` silences them by their prefix, such as ``viewcode`` or ``inheritance``."
msgstr ""

